 - **Money.** The script is platform-funded work the learner did not press for: usage feature `explanation_script` (in `FREE_FEATURES`: recorded, never charged), priced at the registry's Gemini or Fireworks rows by `spendTransport`. The voice is the learner's own Play: usage feature `explanation_audio` (charged, `would_charge`), admitted by `elevenSpendTransport` (`learn-paid-transport.js`) at the registry row `elevenlabs | eleven_flash_v2_5 | input_chars` (an estimate row: the list price is per 1,000 characters and the bill is plan credits), behind the paid confirmation (`paidRefusal`: the press sends `confirmed: true`). About 0.3 cent for a script (twice that when the re-ask runs) and 1.7 to 7 cents for a voice of 430 to 1,800 characters. The first Play asks first: a confirmation (`ConfirmDialog`, "Make the audio", Cancel and Generate) says "This uses paid generation. Estimated cost: N AI units" with the shared `usageLine` wording; N is the server's `voice_estimate_credits` (registry row, rounded up) kept on the card as `narration.estimate_credits`, and without it the dialog says "Price not available yet" and offers no Generate. A card whose script step failed makes the free script first and then asks.
 - **Guards.** Per-user hour and day caps (`admitUsage`, categories `explanation_script` 60 / 200 and `explanation_audio` 30 / 100; a worker var of the same name, for example `EXPLANATION_AUDIO_HOUR`, overrides one) counted only when a real call is about to be made; the platform spend guard and the learner's allowance (`admitSpend`); owner-only access (`authorizedBoardApp` then `subscriptionOwnerRefusal`), so a visitor of a shared or published canvas has no route to either call and the pill draws only for a ready narration (`ExplanationHost.narrate` exists only where the card can be edited).
 - **Idempotency.** One script per (org, canvas, card id) in the isolate, and two requests in flight share one call. The voice is kept as a file source of the board's owner under a deterministic id from (org, canvas, card id, script hash): a second Play, or a click while it is generating, finds the file or shares the in-flight call and is not billed twice. Across isolates (two tabs) a 15-second in-flight marker per file id (one `shared_ask_events` row, category `explanation_audio_inflight`, inserted atomically only when none is younger than 15 s; the paid routes keep no KV and use D1 for coordination) makes the second Play wait, polling the saved file about every second for up to 20 s, then return it; a failure releases the marker, and a marker with no file after 20 s answers `in_progress`. Rows are not pruned. A retry runs only the step that failed (the pill's error state; a failed voice keeps its script).
